1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,173
Las Vegas has a beach, with two thousand seven hundred tons of real sand, and hotel guests get in free.

2
00:00:07,223 --> 00:00:14,473
It is at the Mandalay Bay, on the southern end of the Strip, and it is made for couples and friends who want a pool day and a big night out.

3
00:00:14,523 --> 00:00:19,991
Eleven acres of beach and water, eighteen restaurants, and a casino, all on one property.

4
00:00:20,041 --> 00:00:24,712
Here is how I would plan your stay, and my honest score comes at the end.

5
00:00:24,762 --> 00:00:25,904
Start at the beach.

6
00:00:25,954 --> 00:00:32,503
There is a wave pool with one point six million gallons of water, and a lazy river that loops through the palm trees.

7
00:00:32,553 --> 00:00:40,700
Seven hundred twelve guest reviews single out the pool area, and a hundred twenty-six more praise the beach, the lazy river, and the wave pool.

8
00:00:40,750 --> 00:00:46,459
Expedia lists beach towels, loungers, and umbrellas, plus cabanas if you want more space.

9
00:00:46,509 --> 00:00:50,132
A heated pool and two hot tubs round out the day.

10
00:00:50,182 --> 00:00:51,494
Now, dinner.

11
00:00:51,544 --> 00:00:57,233
The Mandalay Bay has eighteen restaurants, eleven bars and lounges, and three coffee shops.

12
00:00:57,283 --> 00:01:03,900
For steak, there is Strip Steak, and for Mediterranean seafood there is Orla, both from chef Michael Mina.

13
00:01:03,950 --> 00:01:09,275
Libertine Social is the casual pick, open daily for dinner from four to ten.

14
00:01:09,325 --> 00:01:15,315
Citizens Kitchen and Bar is the comfort food spot, with breakfast, sandwiches, and entrees.

15
00:01:15,364 --> 00:01:21,552
Guests love the food: five hundred forty-one reviews call the dining options plentiful and great.

16
00:01:21,602 --> 00:01:26,680
Breakfast cooked to order is served from seven to eleven in the morning, for a fee.

17
00:01:26,730 --> 00:01:27,884
Now, where you sleep.

18
00:01:27,934 --> 00:01:33,301
Rooms have premium bedding, a laptop-friendly workspace, and a forty-two inch TV.

19
00:01:33,352 --> 00:01:37,267
Bathrooms come with designer toiletries and deep soaking tubs.

20
00:01:37,317 --> 00:01:41,297
Some rooms look out over the Strip, and the suites add a separate living room.

21
00:01:41,347 --> 00:01:46,615
Guests rate the rooms clean and comfortable, and cleanliness scores nine out of ten.

22
00:01:46,665 --> 00:01:47,800
Then, the fun part.

23
00:01:47,851 --> 00:01:55,906
The casino covers one hundred thirty-five thousand square feet, with twelve hundred slot machines and one hundred thirty-two gaming tables.

24
00:01:55,956 --> 00:01:59,012
There is a sportsbook too, and a VIP room.

25
00:01:59,062 --> 00:02:03,923
Spa Mandalay has twenty treatment rooms, hot stone massages, and a sauna.

26
00:02:03,973 --> 00:02:09,389
Shark Reef is a twelve-minute walk away, and Allegiant Stadium is fifteen.

27
00:02:09,439 --> 00:02:11,249
A few things to know before you go.

28
00:02:11,299 --> 00:02:17,404
There is a resort fee, and Expedia says it covers the fitness center, internet, and phone calls.

29
00:02:17,454 --> 00:02:22,458
Parking is twenty dollars a day if you park yourself, and forty with valet.

30
00:02:22,508 --> 00:02:26,749
Check-in starts at three in the afternoon, and you must be twenty-one to book.

31
00:02:26,799 --> 00:02:33,219
The beach and wave pool are seasonal, and the pool area runs nine to five in the cooler months, so check your dates.

32
00:02:33,269 --> 00:02:35,280
Cabanas cost extra.

33
00:02:35,330 --> 00:02:37,775
So, is the Mandalay Bay worth it?

34
00:02:37,825 --> 00:02:44,985
On Expedia, guests give it eight point six out of ten, from more than nineteen thousand verified reviews.

35
00:02:45,035 --> 00:02:49,590
Cleanliness scores nine out of ten, and staff and service eight point six.

36
00:02:49,640 --> 00:02:52,300
My honest score is eight and a half out of ten.

37
00:02:52,350 --> 00:02:59,325
It is a great fit for couples and friends who want a real beach day, great dinners, and a big weekend on the Strip.

38
00:02:59,375 --> 00:03:01,400
The link is in the description.
